## Heuristic Quality Filters

The corpora used to train language models are cleaned with simple rules about each document: how
many words it has, how long they are, how many of its lines are bullet points or repeat an earlier
line, and whether it has common words like *the* and *of*. The
[`pb.text.heuristic_filters()`](`pointblank.text.heuristic_filters`) function makes a validation
step for each of the quality filters of the Gopher models, with their bounds as the defaults. It
returns a [`Steps`](`pointblank.Steps`) collection, which is added to a validation with
`add_steps()`. Our documents are short, so we'll lower the number of words that a document needs.

::: {#9733d10b .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
validation = (
    pb.Validate(data=corpus, tbl_name="corpus")
    .add_steps(pb.text.heuristic_filters("text", min_words=10))
    .interrogate()
)

validation
```

