Each rule is a `col_vals_scored()` step with a [`text_stat()`](`pointblank.scorers.text_stat`)
scorer, so the report shows what each one checks and how many documents fail it. The menu has too
few words, repeats its lines, and has too few common words, and the list of hashtags has too many
symbols for its words. The document in French fails the check of common words too, since the
default stop words are English (use `stop_words=` for other languages). Any rule can be turned off
by setting its bound to `None`, and since each is an ordinary step, it can be changed like any
other.

## Near Duplicates

A document that's in a corpus many times gets too much weight in training. The `rows_distinct()`
method finds rows that are exactly the same, but most duplicates in text differ a little: a changed
date, a different footer, or a name filled into a template. The `rows_near_distinct()` method finds
those too. It normalizes the text (in lower case, without punctuation), and with the default
`method="minhash"`, it finds texts whose sequences of words are mostly the same.

::: {#0ba650af .cell execution_count=4}
``` {.python .cell-code}
validation = (
    pb.Validate(data=corpus, tbl_name="corpus")
    .rows_near_distinct(columns="text", threshold=0.8)
    .interrogate()
)

validation.get_step_report(i=1)
```

